<!-- Main Layout Grid -->
<main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 grid grid-cols-1 xl:grid-cols-12 gap-12">
    
    <!-- Left Column: Content -->
    <div class="xl:col-span-8 bg-white p-6 md:p-14 rounded-3xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden relative z-10">
        
        <!-- Article Header -->
        <header class="mb-10 text-center md:text-left">
            <span class="inline-block py-1.5 px-4 rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-5 border border-blue-100">
                Verification Step <%= step %> of <%= totalSteps %>
            </span>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-6 tracking-tight">
                The Ultimate Guide to Personal Finance: Building Wealth in 2026
            </h1>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center md:justify-start space-x-4 mt-6">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560250097-0b93528c311a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=150&h=150&q=80" alt="Author Profile" class="w-full h-full object-cover">
                </div>
                <div>
                    <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-sm">Editorial Team</p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-medium">Updated for 2026</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Header Ad -->
        <div class="ad-wrapper">
            <span class="ad-label">Advertisement</span>
            <div class="ad-slot ad-rectangle">[ Header Ad Slot ]</div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 1: VERIFICATION TIMER BOX -->
        <div class="verify-box flex flex-col items-center justify-center my-12 relative z-20" id="step1-box">
            <div class="bg-green-100 text-green-600 w-20 h-20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mb-6 shadow-inner">
                <svg class="w-10 h-10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"></path>
                </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-2 text-center tracking-tight">Securing Your Connection...</h3>
            
            <!-- Timer Area -->
            <div id="timer-wrapper" class="w-full flex justify-center">
                <div class="text-7xl font-black text-blue-600 my-4 h-24 flex items-center justify-center tracking-tighter drop-shadow-sm" id="timerDisplay">10</div>
            </div>
            <p id="instructionText" class="text-sm md:text-base font-bold text-gray-500 mb-8 animate-pulse h-6 text-center">Checking browser security before proceeding...</p>
            
            <!-- Scroll Button with SVG Arrow -->
            <a href="#bottom-verify-section" id="scroll-btn" class="hidden w-full max-w-md mx-auto bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600 to-indigo-600 text-white font-bold py-4 px-6 rounded-2xl shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all flex items-center justify-center text-lg mt-2 relative z-50 clickable-btn border border-blue-400 border-opacity-30">
                Scroll Down To Continue
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 ml-2 animate-bounce" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"></path></svg>
            </a>
        </div>

        <!-- FULL ARTICLE CONTENT RESTORED & ENHANCED -->
        <article class="article-body mt-12">
            <p class="drop-cap">Money management in 2026 is more important than ever before. As the costs of living increase, digital financial services evolve, the labor markets shift, and access to credit becomes dangerously simple, novices can easily have a panic attack when working to establish financial security.</p>
            
            <!-- IMAGE 1: High-Quality Stable Image with hover wrapper & fallback -->
            <div class="image-wrapper">
                <img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1579621970563-ebec7560ff3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=675&q=80" alt="Financial Planning and Analysis" class="article-image" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611162617474-5b21e879e113?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=675&q=80';">
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">Strategic planning is the unshakable foundation of wealth generation.</p>
            
            <h2>1. Developing a Bulletproof Budgeting Routine</h2>
            <p>Personal finance is firmly rooted in budgeting. Contrary to popular belief, budgeting is not a constraint on your life; it merely makes your money organized so you can deploy it like a highly-effective tool. Beginners should develop a realistic budget utilizing the 50/30/20 rule: 50% for necessities, 30% for wants, and 20% strictly for savings and investments.</p>
            
            <!-- IMAGE 2: High-Quality Stable Image -->
            <div class="image-wrapper">
                <img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224155-8d04cb21cd6c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=675&q=80" alt="Budgeting tools and calculators" class="article-image" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611162617474-5b21e879e113?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=675&q=80';">
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">Track every penny to ensure your daily budget aligns with your long-term goals.</p>
            
            <!-- Article Ad 1 -->
            <div class="ad-wrapper">
                <span class="ad-label">Advertisement</span>
                <div class="ad-slot ad-rectangle">[ Article Ad Slot 1 ]</div>
            </div>
            
            <h2>2. The Psychology of Saving Money</h2>
            <p>You shouldn't wait until you "make more money" to start saving; saving is a priority that creates wealth over time, regardless of income. Small, automated, and regular savings do wonders thanks to compound interest. With digital wallets and auto-transfer features in 2026, you can easily set your bank to move 10% of your paycheck into a savings account before you even see it.</p>
            
            <!-- IMAGE 3: High-Quality Stable Image -->
            <div class="image-wrapper">
                <img loading="lazy" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1607863680198-23d4b2565df0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=675&q=80" alt="Piggy Bank Saving Money" class="article-image" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611162617474-5b21e879e113?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&h=675&q=80';">
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">Automating your savings makes building an emergency fund completely effortless.</p>
            
            <h2>3. Mastering Debt and Credit Scores</h2>
            <p>Not all debt is bad, but unmanaged consumer debt is a wealth destroyer. Focus on eliminating high-interest liabilities, such as credit card balances, using the Avalanche method (paying highest interest first) or the Snowball method (paying smallest balances first for psychological wins). Maintaining a pristine credit score will unlock the lowest borrowing rates when you actually need them.</p>
            
            <!-- Article Ad 2 -->
            <div class="ad-wrapper">
                <span class="ad-label">Advertisement</span>
                <div class="ad-slot ad-rectangle">[ Article Ad Slot 2 ]</div>
            </div>
            
            <h2>4. Creating Multiple Revenue Streams</h2>
            <p>Depending on a single source of income is the riskiest financial decision you can make today. The world is experiencing rapid transformations in job markets, fueled by AI and automation. Building multiple streams of income—whether it's dividend investing, freelance consulting, creating digital products, or real estate—creates a protective moat around your lifestyle.</p>
            
            <h2>5. Fundamentals of Investing</h2>
            <p>Investing is not the prerogative of Wall Street experts. Today, anyone can access index funds, ETFs, and robo-advisors directly from their smartphone. The key is understanding that time in the market consistently beats timing the market. Begin with low-risk, broad-market index funds (like the S&P 500) and let compounding do the heavy lifting over decades.</p>
            
            <h2>Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Personal finance in 2026 is about consistency, emotional discipline, and automation. You must prioritize organization over complex strategies. By mastering budgeting, wiping out toxic debt, securing multiple income streams, and investing for the long horizon, you are laying an unshakable foundation for true financial freedom.</p>
        </article>

        <!-- STEP 2: FINAL CONTINUE BUTTON -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-3xl p-10 text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center shadow-inner relative z-20" id="bottom-verify-section">
